						"description": "Reports a publish, consume or fail of a task within a workflow instance. The engine checks the report against the task state machine in docs/contract.md; every transition is atomic.\n\n**Required query parameters:**\n\n1. workflow_instance_id: the id returned by start_instance\n2. action_type: publish | consume | fail\n3. event_name: the task topic as declared in the DSL\n4. is_retry: true | false (case-insensitive; anything else is 400). true makes a duplicate report idempotent (200, no change) instead of a 409; it never unlocks a forbidden transition.\n5. service_name: the consuming service; required for consume and fail\n\n**Body (publish only):** the message payload, a JSON object. It is stored on the task and carried by the failure webhook.\n\n**Responses (all JSON):**\n\n- 200 - `{\"workflow_instance_id\", \"task_index\", \"task_state\", \"workflow_state\", \"idempotent\"}`; task_index/task_state are arrays when a publish resolved several tasks sharing a topic\n- 400 - MISSING_PARAM | INVALID_PARAM | INVALID_BODY\n- 404 - INSTANCE_NOT_FOUND | TASK_NOT_FOUND\n- 409 - TASK_NOT_PUBLISHED | TASK_ALREADY_PUBLISHED | TASK_ALREADY_COMPLETED | TASK_ALREADY_FAILED | INSTANCE_TERMINAL\n- 500 - INTERNAL (Redis error; retry)\n\nError bodies: `{\"error\": \"<code>\", \"message\": \"...\"}`."
